{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00336","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00336@rel:R25-11#58b5b3b7","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00336","release":"R25-11","content":"function ResetAllFiles [SWS_PER_00336] Upstream: RS_PER_00001 , RS_PER_00004 , RS_PER_00009 , RS_PER_00010 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_AP_00121 , RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00128 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00137 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; ResetAllFiles (const ara::core::Instance Specifier &amp;fs) noexcept; Resets a File Storage, including all files. ResetAllFiles resets a File Storage to the initial state, containing only the files which were deployed from the Target Configuration, with their initial content. Afterwards, the File Storage will appear as if it was newly installed from the current Target Configuration. It will fail with kResourceBusy when the File Storage is currently open, or when it is modified by a call from another thread to UpdatePersistency, CleanUpPersistency, ResetPersistency, RecoverAllFiles, or ResetAllFiles. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/file_storage.h\" class mono Scope namespace ara::per class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe PerErrc ::kStorageNot rollback_semantics class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td fs td The shortName path of a PortPrototype typed by a PersistencyFile StorageInterface. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; td A Result of void. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td Found td Returned if the passed InstanceSpecifier does not match any PersistencyFileStorageInterface configured for this Executable. td PerErrc ::kPhysicalStorageFailure td no_rollback_semantics Returned if access to the physical storage fails. td PerErrc ::kEncryptionFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the encryption of stored data fails. td PerErrc ::kResourceBusy td rollback_semantics Returned if UpdatePersistency, CleanUpPersistency, or Reset Persistency is currently being executed, or if RecoverAllFiles is currently being executed for the same File Storage, or a Shared Handle of the same File Storage is currently in use. td PerErrc ::kOutOfStorageSpace td no_rollback_semantics Returned if the available physical storage space is insufficient for the initial files. td PerErrc ::kAuthenticationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if calculating the MAC of stored data fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00336","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11"],"platform_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11"},"element":{"kind":"function","name":"ResetAllFiles","module":"PER","cluster":"","page":"namespaces/ns_per_ara_per_d9a3e9.html","doc_type":"SWS","ai":false,"first":"R25-11","last":"R25-11","changed":[],"distinct":1,"universe":"AP"},"evidence":{"figures":[{"id":"FIG-90dbf15c08d6f936","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_EXP_SWArchitecture","p":87,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.85,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"ResetAllFiles API in Persistency","n":9,"cap":"Figure 9.35: Interfaces for file storage","sha":"90dbf15c08d6f936c170554e8c7a2f77567241569f8f890405bc3996341e9929","nser":5,"src":"figure"},{"id":"SNIP_ADAPTIVE_PLATFORM_FIGURE_Figure_12_6","doc":"TPS_ManifestSpecification","p":561,"rel":[],"role":"heuristic","conf":0.75,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Reset initial content from deployment configuration","n":3,"cap":"Figure 12.6","sha":null,"nser":1,"src":"manifest"}],"snippets":[{"id":"SNIP_per_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_P_P116_340","doc":"A